  // X: Beyond the Frontier's sector map. games/xtension has its own.
  //
  // name, xbtfTextId, x and y are the game's own: the text tables name every sector, and the text
  // id encodes its cell (2YX in XBTF; x runs east, y south, from 1).
  //
  // race and gates are not in any game file decoded so far (the universe is set up by the compiled
  // script, l/001.obj). They are read from elite-games.ru's map: xbtf.png,
  // by sampling each cell's colour and the midpoint of every shared edge, where a wall is black
  // background and a gate is not. Gates are symmetric; each lists the directions it opens to.
  //
  // stations come from the same site's Excel map (mapxbtf.rar), which places station codes
  // inside each sector. Codes are read by the sector's race (N1 in an Argon sector is the wheat
  // farm, in a Boron one the plankton farm). Its unexplained markers (*, + and one V in an
  // enemy sector) are skipped. A station of another race inside a sector would be misread;
  // the map gives no way to tell.
  //
